---
id: org.dxos.plugin.streamDeck
name: StreamDeckPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

Projects a Composer space onto Stream Deck hardware: the space's favorites on the keys, running
tasks or space statistics on the dials.

The device itself is driven by a separate Elgato plugin (`@dxos/composer-stream-deck`), because
Elgato's application holds the HID device exclusively while it runs. This plugin is the brain: it
builds the model from ECHO, renders every key as an SVG string, and publishes frames over a loopback
WebSocket. Design: `agents/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-stream-deck-design.md`.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`       |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`       |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`       |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`  |
| `flow`      | `org.dxos.mdl.flow@1.0`       |

## Types

```mdl
type DeviceProfile
  desc: Physical characteristics of a Stream Deck model, reported by the device plugin.
  fields:
    model: string
    keys: number
    dials: number
    keySize: [number, number]     # key image size in pixels
    dialSize: [number, number]    # touch-strip segment size, one per dial
```

```mdl
type Shortcut
  desc: What one key shows. Produced by the model, consumed by the renderer; never crosses the wire.
  fields:
    target: string                # graph navigation path; the press target
    label: string
    icon: string                  # sprite icon name, e.g. ph--house--regular
    hue?: string                  # chromatic palette name
```

```mdl
type MetricSpec
  desc: What one touch-strip segment shows — a running task, or a statistic when nothing is running.
  fields:
    kind: progress | stat
    title: string
    ratio?: number                # progress only; absent when the task reports no total
    detail?: string               # progress only
    value?: string                # stat only
```

```mdl
type SpaceStats
  fields:
    objects: number
    feeds: number
    types: number
    plugins: number
```

```mdl
type KeyImage
  desc: One rendered key on the wire. Elgato's setImage accepts SVG, so nothing is rasterised.
  fields:
    svg: string
    target?: string               # echoed back with a press, so the device stays stateless
```

```mdl
type DialFeedback
  desc: One touch-strip segment on the wire, expressed semantically rather than as an Elgato layout.
  fields:
    title: string
    value: string
    bar?: number                  # fraction in [0, 1]
```

```mdl
type Frame
  desc: The full display state. A null slot is cleared.
  fields:
    keys: KeyImage?[]
    dials: DialFeedback?[]
```

```mdl
type BridgeStatus
  desc: Live connection state, published so surfaces can read it without opening a connection.
  fields:
    state: idle | connecting | connected | incompatible
    device?: DeviceProfile
```

## Components

```mdl
component VirtualStreamDeck
  desc: On-screen replica rendering the very frame the device is sent, so the two cannot drift.
```

```mdl
component StreamDeckStatus
  desc: Rail indicator, rendered only while a device is attached.
```

```mdl
component StreamDeckDashboard
  desc: Space-level deck companion previewing the hardware; renders the frame but does not send it.
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Favorites on the keys

  req F-1.1: A key shows an object carrying the space's `favorite` ECHO tag, with its icon and name.
  req F-1.2: The favorite tag is resolved by label among keyless tags; a keyed provider tag labelled
    "favorite" belongs to that provider and is ignored.
  req F-1.3: Slots are filled from a stable sort (label, then path); positions are not persisted.
  req F-1.4: A favorite with no derivable navigation path is dropped rather than shown as a dead key.
  req F-1.5: Pressing a key opens that object and brings the window forward.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Monitors and statistics on the dials

  req F-2.1: While any task is pending or running, each segment shows one task with a progress bar.
  req F-2.2: A task reporting no total shows as indeterminate rather than as zero progress.
  req F-2.3: With nothing running, the segments show the space's object, feed, type and plugin counts.
  req F-2.4: Finished and failed tasks do not occupy a segment.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Rendering

  req F-3.1: A key is rendered as an SVG string at the device's pixel size, with the icon inlined from
    the app's sprite — a sprite reference cannot resolve outside the document.
  req F-3.2: Labels are wrapped to two lines and ellipsised; every interpolated label is XML-escaped.
  req F-3.3: Colours are literal, because the device cannot resolve the theme's CSS custom properties.
  req F-3.4: The panel and the device are sent the identical frame.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: The bridge

  req F-4.1: Composer dials into the device plugin, which listens; a browser tab cannot accept
    connections, and the Elgato-hosted process outlives any Composer window.
  req F-4.2: A failed connection is the normal case (most users have no device plugin) and retries
    quietly with backoff from 1s to 30s, surfacing no error.
  req F-4.3: A protocol version mismatch stops rather than reconnecting, since a retry cannot fix it.
  req F-4.4: A frame identical to the last one is not published.
  req F-4.5: Exactly one bridge exists — the headless driver owns it, and surfaces read
    `BridgeStatus` instead of connecting themselves.
  req F-4.6: The driver runs with no surface rendered, so the keys stay live with the panel closed.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
test T-1: Favorites appear in a stable order
  given: a space with objects tagged `favorite`, one of them added after the others
  then: the keys are ordered by label, and adding a favorite does not reorder the others by chance
```

```mdl
test T-2: A provider tag does not masquerade as the favorite tag
  given: a tag labelled "favorite" carrying a foreign key
  then: no favorites are shown
```

```mdl
test T-3: A running task takes over the strip
  given: a pending or running progress task and a space with statistics
  then: the first segment shows the task with a bar, and the remaining segments are cleared
```

```mdl
test T-4: The device shows the offline state when Composer is absent
  given: the device plugin running with no client connected
  then: every placed key and dial renders the offline state
```

```mdl
test T-5: A press reaches Composer with its slot
  given: two Favorite keys placed at columns 0 and 1
  when: the key at column 1 is pressed
  then: Composer receives a keyDown for slot 1 and opens the object that key was showing
```

```mdl
test T-6: An incompatible device plugin does not loop
  given: a device plugin announcing a different protocol version
  then: the bridge reports `incompatible` and makes no further connection attempts
```

---

## QA

Executable flows. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by flow and step number.

```mdl
flow QA-1: A favorite appears on the virtual deck
  desc: |
    The part of the round-trip observable without Stream Deck hardware: tag an object as a
    favorite and confirm it renders on `VirtualStreamDeck`, the on-screen replica that is sent
    the identical frame as the device (F-3.4). This plugin declares no operations of its own —
    favoriting goes through `space.addTag`, owned by `plugin-space`.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.3, F-3.1, F-3.4, T-1]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - plugin-stream-deck is enabled — it is `isDev`-gated both for availability and in defaults
      (`plugin-defs.tsx`: `isDev && StreamDeckPlugin.make()`), so it is OFF outside dev builds
    - document: a Document named "QA Favorite" already exists in the space, with no `favorite`
      tag on it — ABORT rather than tagging or deleting one this flow did not create
    - favoriteTag: a keyless Tag object labelled "favorite" (query for one before creating
      another, per `SpaceOperation.AddTag`'s own guidance)
  test:
    - name: Tag the document as a favorite
      do: Right-click "QA Favorite" in the navtree and choose "Add to favorites" (or apply the
        `favorite` tag from the tag picker).
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addTag { tag: $given.favoriteTag, object: $given.document }
      capture: tagged
      expect: "QA Favorite" carries a keyless tag labelled "favorite"
      assert: return $tagged.object.tags?.some((t) => t.label === 'favorite' && !t.key);
      note: |
        MUST be keyless — F-1.2 says a keyed provider tag also labelled "favorite" belongs to
        that provider and is ignored, so this step's assert is the one place that distinction is
        falsifiable.
    - name: Open the deck dashboard
      do: Open the space's Stream Deck companion panel (StreamDeckDashboard).
      expect: VirtualStreamDeck shows a key labelled "QA Favorite" with its document icon
      note: |
        NO invoke — VirtualStreamDeck is a read-only render of the same model the bridge sends
        (F-3.4); there is no operation to invoke, only a surface to observe.
    - name: Press the key on the virtual deck
      do: Click the "QA Favorite" key in VirtualStreamDeck.
      expect: "QA Favorite" opens and its window comes forward (F-1.5)
  after:
    - name: Remove the favorite tag
      do: Right-click "QA Favorite" and remove the "favorite" tag.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeTag { tag: $given.favoriteTag, object: $given.document }
      expect: the key no longer appears on VirtualStreamDeck
```

```mdl
flow QA-2: Real hardware round-trip
  desc: The device-attached path — a real Stream Deck key press reaching Composer.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-4.1, F-4.5, T-5]
  status: blocked
  given:
    - the `@dxos/composer-stream-deck` Elgato plugin is installed and a physical Stream Deck is
      attached
    - Composer is running with plugin-stream-deck enabled and has at least one favorite placed
  test:
    - name: Press a physical key
      do: Press the key showing a favorite on the physical device.
      expect: Composer receives the keyDown for that slot and opens the object that key was
        showing (T-5)
      blocked: |
        Requires physical Stream Deck hardware and the separate Elgato-hosted process holding the
        HID device (F-4.1) — neither the debug port nor this repo's dev tooling can simulate a
        HID key press. Per Execution Rule 9, the flow's status is `blocked`, not `failing`.
  after:
    - name: No teardown
      do: No ECHO state is created by a key press; nothing to undo.
      expect: the deck returns to its idle page with the favorite still bound
```

